  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mesoamerica Critical Forest Biome IP Regional Coordination, Knowledge Sharing and Support Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Regional Coordination and Technical Support Project (RCP) does not directly contribute to the GEF Core Indicator, as its role is to reinforce the impacts of country projects. The only contribution of the RCP is on Core Indicator 11 which includes the participants in the capacity building technical support provided. The RCP will promote equal gender participation to ensure that at least 35% of the beneficiaries are women.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To conserve Mesoamerica primary forests through strengthened governance, protection, restoration, regional cooperation, and the mobilization of stable long-term funding, ensuring a sustainable flow of ecosystem services for people and planet</narrative>
  </description>
